              "author": "endocrinology",
              "date": "2022-02-09T08:15",
              "body": "ENDOCRINOLOGY FOLLOW-UP — 2/7/2022\n\nMs. Zhang returns three months into methimazole for Graves disease. Palpitations gone, sleeping normally, appetite back to baseline and weight coming back up. No rash, fevers or sore throats. No itching or dark urine.\n\nVitals: HR 76. Exam: no tremor, goiter smaller and soft, no eye signs.\n\nLabs today: TSH 0.9 mIU/L, free T4 1.2 ng/dL. Your 12/20 values reviewed.\n\nAssessment: Graves disease, now euthyroid on methimazole 10 mg.\nPlan: Reduce to methimazole 5 mg daily. TFTs every 3-4 months for the first year, can be done with primary care. We will see her yearly. Continue to watch liver enzymes given chronic hepatitis B.\n\nAllergies: NKDA. Medications: methimazole 5 mg daily.\n\nEndocrinology"
            }
          ],
