          "documents": [
            {
              "type": "Progress Notes",
              "title": "Annual Physical",
              "author": "PCP",
              "date": "2022-09-21T08:30",
              "body": "Annual exam.\n\nSince last physical: diagnosed with Graves disease last fall, on methimazole, now 5 mg daily per endocrinology. Feels back to herself. Weight back up close to her old baseline. No sore throats or fevers. No rash.\nMigraines: two or three this year, same pattern, home measures.\nNo GI symptoms. Coaching again this season.\n\nMeds: methimazole 5 mg daily. NKDA.\n\nExam: Vitals as charted. Calm, no tremor. Thyroid mildly full, smooth, non-tender. No proptosis. Heart regular, no murmur. Lungs clear. Abdomen soft, no hepatosplenomegaly. Skin warm and dry, no rash. Ext no edema.\nPHQ-2: 0.\n\nA/P\n1. Graves disease on methimazole 5 mg: TFTs today; CBC with diff given the drug.\n2. Chronic hepatitis B: CMP for liver enzymes.\n3. Migraine without aura: stable.\n4. Prevention: Pap current through 2023. Flu shot today. Bivalent COVID booster at pharmacy when she can.\n\nOne year."
            }
          ]
