            {
              "type": "Consult Note",
              "title": "Endocrinology Follow-up",
              "author": "endocrinology",
              "date": "2023-01-26T10:05",
              "body": "Endocrinology annual follow-up, 1/23/23.\n\nGraves disease, about 14 months on methimazole, on 5 mg daily for nearly a year. Clinically euthyroid. No side effects. Normal TFTs in May and December (drawn at your office), and normal CBC and liver tests in September.\n\nExam: HR regular, no tremor, small smooth goiter, no orbitopathy.\n\nWe talked about how long to continue. With a goiter still present she is willing to stay on low-dose methimazole for now rather than stop and risk relapse; long-term low-dose therapy is a reasonable option. RAI and thyroidectomy remain alternatives if she ever wants definitive treatment.\n\nPlan: continue methimazole 5 mg daily. TFTs every 4-6 months. Return 1 year.\n\nEndocrinology"
            }
          ]
