            {
              "type": "Progress Notes",
              "title": "Annual Physical",
              "author": "PCP",
              "date": "2023-09-27T08:40",
              "body": "Annual. 30 now.\n\nInterval: Graves stable on methimazole 5 mg; endo in January kept her on it long term. Feels well. One missed lab in June, made up a week later, normal.\nMigraine: a few this year, nothing new about them.\nNo abdominal pain, no jaundice, no dark urine.\nBusy start of the school year, otherwise fine. Mood good.\n\nMeds: methimazole 5 mg daily. Allergies: NKDA.\n\nExam: Vitals as charted. Well, no tremor. Small smooth goiter, unchanged, no nodules. No proptosis. Heart RRR, no murmur. Lungs clear. Abd soft, no HSM. Pelvic: normal; Pap with HPV collected. Skin normal.\nPHQ-2: 1.\n\nA/P\n1. Graves disease: TFTs. CBC.\n2. Chronic hep B: CMP for LFTs.\n3. Migraine without aura: stable.\n4. Cervical screening: co-test today (now 30), then every 5 years if negative.\n5. Flu today. Updated COVID shot at the pharmacy.\n\nRTC 1 yr."
            }
